{% doc %}
  Splices in-grid banner blocks into a product loop.

  ## The problem it solves

  Banners are blocks, products come from a paginated collection, and the two
  have to interleave. Rendering all the products and then all the banners puts
  every banner at the end; rendering banners inside the product loop means
  re-scanning the block list on every iteration.

  This snippet does the scan once per product index, which is the cheapest
  correct option in Liquid — there are no hashes, so a lookup table cannot be
  built ahead of time.

  ## Position is per page, not per collection

  A banner set to position 5 appears after the fifth product *on every page*,
  not after the fifth product in the collection. That is the behaviour a
  merchant configuring "a banner a third of the way down the grid" expects, and
  it is the only one that survives filtering — with 200 products filtered to 4,
  a collection-absolute position 30 would render nothing at all.

  @param {object} section
  @param {number} index - The 1-based position of the product just rendered

  @example
    {%- for product in collection.products -%}
      <li>{% render 'product-card', product: product %}</li>
      {% render 'grid-banners', section: section, index: forloop.index %}
    {%- endfor -%}
{% enddoc %}

{%- for block in section.blocks -%}
  {%- if block.type == 'grid-banner' -%}
    {%- assign banner_position = block.settings.position | plus: 0 -%}
    {%- if banner_position == index -%}
      {% comment %} {% content_for 'block', id: block.id %} {% endcomment %}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
